  "_buses": "A cue can name a bus, and the bus level multiplies it. The three voice lines are recordings of a person among 50ms impacts: they need balancing against the effects as a GROUP. Measured, not guessed — each line's gain is set from the RMS of its loudest half so all three land at -15.7 dBFS out. The bus sits above 1 so no single gain has to.",
  "buses": {
    "voice": 1.25
  },
  "voiceDuck": 0.5,
  "_voiceDuck": "While a voice line is sounding, every other cue starts at half level. A line is a person talking and the game does not stop for it: a wave of towers firing over the top is what makes one unintelligible. Nothing is cut off — Phaser mixes rather than steals voices — so this only moves what starts DURING the line, which is the case that matters, since the effects are all short and restarting constantly."
